spec.entry_signal:
ONE entry-signal function, `mulham_sweep_m1(close, high, low, vol, i, g)`, no-lookahead (uses only [:i+1]), reusing FRIDAY's audited helpers. It is a SWEEP-RECLAIM of a session extreme (the four reports converge on this: the "rectangle" = a session high/low; the M1 trigger = sweep-then-body-close-reclaim). I deliberately REJECT the alternate "EMA200-pullback" reading (report 2) and "consolidation box break-and-retest" reading (report 3) as the PRIMARY genome, because FRIDAY already ships `multi_trader.WICK_REV_CONF=0.70` + `ms.sweep_level()` (the sweep-reclaim path), and the consolidated 21-indicator vote IS the break-and-retest's directional logic — so sweep-reclaim is the only variant that is genuinely NEW vs what's already in-house. The other two should be added only as GA `sweep_confirm`/archetype sub-genes, not as the core.

EXACT FUNCTION (drop into a new r_native_v2/genome_factory archetype branch; helpers _ema/_rsi/_atr already exist in chart_read.py and dynamic_stop.py):

```
def _session_extreme(times, high, low, i, sess_name):
    # objective rectangle anchor: prior completed session's hi/lo (NO discretion, NO lookahead).
    # uses indicators/session.classify on bar timestamps[:i] only.
    from indicators import session as S
    from datetime import datetime, timezone
    cur = S.classify(datetime.fromtimestamp(int(times[i]), tz=timezone.utc)).name
    hi=lo=None; saw=False
    for k in range(i-1, max(0,i-600), -1):       # walk back to the PRIOR block of `sess_name`
        nm = S.classify(datetime.fromtimestamp(int(times[k]), tz=timezone.utc)).name
        if nm == sess_name:
            saw=True; hi = high[k] if hi is None else max(hi,high[k]); lo = low[k] if lo is None else min(lo,low[k])
        elif saw:
            break                                 # finished the prior session block
    return (hi, lo) if (hi is not None and cur != sess_name) else (None,None)

def mulham_sweep_m1(close, high, low, vol, times, i, g):
    # returns (dir, conf, sl_px, box_lo, box_hi) or (0,...). dir at bar i from close[:i+1] ONLY.
    if i < 60: return (0,0.0,None,None,None)
    hi, lo = _session_extreme(times, high, low, i, g.get("sweep_session","NY_OVERLAP"))
    if hi is None: return (0,0.0,None,None,None)
    atr = _atr(high[:i+1], low[:i+1], close[:i+1])           # dynamic_stop._atr (audited)
    if atr <= 0: return (0,0.0,None,None,None)
    nb   = int(g.get("sweep_confirm_bars",3))               # M1 bars for the reclaim
    buf  = float(g.get("sweep_sl_buffer_atr",0.30))*atr     # SL pad past the wick
    rec  = range(max(1,i-nb), i+1)
    # HTF align via EMA50-slope on M1 (window-computable, no D1) — the trend gate
    ema = _ema(close[:i+1],50); up = ema[-1]>ema[-4]; dn = ema[-1]<ema[-4]
    body_dn = close[i] < close[i-1] and close[i] < (close[i]+ (high[i]-low[i]) )*0  # close[i]<open proxy via prev
    # SELL: swept the prior-session HIGH then M1 body closed back BELOW it
    swept_hi = any(high[k] > hi for k in rec); reclaim_dn = close[i] < hi
    if swept_hi and reclaim_dn and ((not g.get("sweep_trend_align",True)) or dn):
        wick = max(high[k] for k in rec); sl = wick + buf
        return (-1, 1.0, sl, lo, hi)
    # BUY: swept the prior-session LOW then M1 body closed back ABOVE it
    swept_lo = any(low[k]  < lo for k in rec); reclaim_up = close[i] > lo
    if swept_lo and reclaim_up and ((not g.get("sweep_trend_align",True)) or up):
        wick = min(low[k] for k in rec); sl = wick - buf
        return (1, 1.0, sl, lo, hi)
    return (0,0.0,None,None,None)
```

Indicators used (all existing): chart_read._ema/_rsi, dynamic_stop._atr, indicators/session.classify. conf is 1.0/0.0 (the sweep IS the conviction, exactly like the box archetype in report 3 — conf_gate then just toggles). For the LIVE path, the same logic is already 90% present: `multi_trader` calls `ms.sweep_level()` + the WICK_REV_CONF block — only the "WHICH level = prior session extreme" constraint is new.
